live-draw: zeta dumps and a geometry-capture spike (diagnostics only, all off by default).

1. LD_SURF_DUMP also writes zetas. At the end of the frame after the dump fires, every tracked zeta's R32F
   snapshot is written as a PFM (f<frame>_zeta_<slot>_<offset>_d<depth fmt>_<w>x<h>.pfm, rows bottom to top) and
   logged as "[zeta-dump] slot=...". During that frame every zeta snapshot a draw samples (shadow compare, X16 value
   or ARGB byte reads) is written when the draw has run (f<frame>_zread_<seq>_u<unit>_...pfm, at most 8 per zeta
   except shadow-compare reads, 64 in all) with the draw's inline fragment constants next to it (.pfm.fpc), so the
   lookup can be recomputed offline. Shadow maps are reused inside a frame, so the state at the present is not the
   one a light read.
   Why (Killzone 3): checking the sun shadow maps (0x2980000 / 0x2DA0000, Z16 1408x1408) against what the deferred
   sun shader computes (RSX pass 25).

2. LD_GEOM_CAPTURE=1 (with LD_SURF_DUMP): in the same frame, the generated vertex shader writes each vertex's guest
   clip position o[0] and its host clip position (Out.pos) to a typed UAV (RWBuffer<float4> u0, root table 5;
   guard constants b2 in root parameter 6: base element, vertex count, on). The root signature only grows when the
   variable is set. Written next to the zeta dumps: geom_meta.tsv (one row per draw: target, zeta, clip, topology,
   counts, PSO key, depth test/write), geom_verts.bin, geom_idx.bin (triangle-list indices of indexed draws), and
   "[geom-cap] frame=... draws=... vertices=..." in the log. 192 MB buffer (6 M vertices); draws past it are counted
   as overflow.
   Why (Killzone 3): the spike (ray-traced shadows/AO need world-space geometry; a recompiled game only has draw
   calls).
